{
  "_readme": [
    "Canned Calendar payloads. Same batching and same UTC-time convention as gmail.json.",
    "",
    "Calendar needs no rollup: one event is one meeting, and it already produces one",
    "touchpoint per external attendee (touchpoints_external_key includes person_id for",
    "exactly this reason). What it needs instead is a set of rules about which attendees",
    "count, because channel = 'meeting' qualifies for promotion — a calendar entry can turn",
    "a watchlist name into an active relationship, and an invitation nobody accepted is not",
    "a meeting that happened."
  ],

  "operator": "derek@seakingcapital.com",

  "batches": [
    [
      {
        "_case": "A real meeting with two external attendees, one accepted and one tentative. Both count. The conference room is an attendee as far as the API is concerned and must not become a person.",
